A||N||19||fropuff||nitrous, etc.||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||05-14-2001||11:48 PM||||You guys are going to really hate me now!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Oh well.  Actually, I've just been thinking of doing a nitrous kit, like before.  I was thinking of doing an NOS kit, an underdrive pulley, an MSD box, cold air intake, and a few other things.  I think this is the best deal for me, and I might actually stay with it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I know I said that I didn't want NOS, but if my 2.8 ever goes, I will still do a 3.4L pushrod.  I was wondering if anyone has any other ideas on what misc. mods I should do if I do an NOS system.  I think the total will even be less than $1000.  Good deal!  Thanks a lot!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||10
Z||000001||MODIFIE||05-15-2001||09:06 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/wwfl.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/wwfl.html</A>   <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/nitrous.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/nitrous.html</A> <P>here a some links on nos the top link is on stealth nos kit on a fiero<P>||||reg||12
Z||000002||fropuff||05-15-2001||09:26 PM||||Thanks for the links.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The first one didn't work for me, but the others did, and they helped.  I did a little search for nitrous, and I came up with a little list of things that I'd get with the NOS kit.  Here it goes...<P>-new fuel pump <BR>-fuel pressure riser<BR>-new plugs, wires, coil, cap<BR>-MSD ignition box<P>I'd also get the cold air intake and maybe a performance auto shift kit.  Let me know what you think.  Thanks a lot!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||10
Z||000003||fropuff||05-15-2001||10:38 PM||||Okay, I did a little rough estimating on the cost of this stuff.  Here goes...<P>-NOS kit (&lt;$500)<BR>-fuel pump ($200)<BR>-Crane HI-6S ($136)<BR>-PS-92 coil ($67)<BR>-cold air intake ($175)<BR>-power pulley kit ($80)<BR>-performance auto shift kit ($35)<BR>-plugs/cap/wires (~$75)<P>All this added together totals around $1250.  Still not bad.  I was expecting under $1000, but this is still relatively cheap.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||05-15-2001||10:42 PM||||Fuel pump won't be that much.  You can get a Corvette LT4 pump for 80 bucks shipped from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||05-16-2001||01:17 AM||||Keep in mind that nitrous is very hard on the bottom end components and the 2.8's have a very weak bottom end to start out with. Its pretty common for bearings, rods, etc. to fail on a stock car with only 100,000 miles on it. In my opinion a 2.8 and nitrous is asking for trouble unless you really just don't care and can drop a new motor in whenever this one eats it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||05-16-2001||07:57 AM||||Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR>"Keep in mind that nitrous is very hard on the bottom end components and the 2.8's have a very weak bottom end to start out with. Its pretty common for bearings, rods, etc. to fail on a stock car with only 100,000 miles on it. In my opinion a 2.8 and nitrous is asking for trouble unless you really just don't care and can drop a new motor in whenever this one eats it."<P>-Well, that was exactly what I was thinking.  My 2.8 now has 63336.0 miles on it, and if the engine ever did anything, I'd just switch over to a 3.4L pushrod Camaro block.  I would only use it maybe 3 or 4 times a week, tops.  The parts I'm planning on using can also be used on the 3.4L.  The only thing that I'd be out on is the NOS system, but it'd be worth it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That's also why I'm upgrading the fuel and ignition sytems as well.  Thanks for the concern though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||05-16-2001||08:09 AM||||tough on the bottom end... yeah but not as bad as you'd think... if you get a nitrous kit get a Nitrous Express kit. <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>   <P>for nitrous info...  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html</A> <P>with only 60,000 miles on your car all you really need to to is the MSd and make sure your injectors are clean... i had 87k on mine when i installed nitrous and 97K when i sold the car and never had a nitrous related engine failure. i kill clutches but that was due to the harsh shot i was running. if you run the included jetting you'll be fine. Shaun41178 has an auto with nitrous and he is very pleased with it... i'll let ya know how my GT Auto install goes. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">      <BR>www.engineered.net<BR>www.epdyno.com<BR>www.enthuzacar.com||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||05-16-2001||04:02 PM||||Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<P>"With only 60,000 miles on your car all you really need to to is the MSD and make sure your injectors are clean."<P>&gt;What about the fuel pump, coil, etc.?  I still plan on doing the performance auto shift kit, the power pulley kit, the MSD (or Crane), and the NOS setup.  What others things do I *need* besides the MSD and clean injectors?  Thanks.<P>"I'll let ya know how my GT Auto install goes."<P>&gt;Yeah, please do that.  When do you plan on doing the install?  I plan on getting the NOS system this fall, so I can try it out w/o the snow.  I don't think nitrous works good in the snow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Thanks!!! <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||sluppy123||05-16-2001||05:28 PM||||I have a NOS kit on my 87 GT auto, I bought it from a forum member that never installed it. I installed it onto a new Jasper preformance 2.8 engine, changed the fuel pump and installed MSD coil, all other parts are stock.<P>I'm very happy with the preformance even with the auto tranny. Although if I were to buy another kit it would be a nitrous express kit. I'm still thinking about buying the kit to convert my Dry NOS kit to a wet system. <P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Eibach springs, RSM side scoops & chin spoiler, Mr Mikes leather, 70hp NOS, & much more.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=12781563&p=48213929&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000010||ferrari_momo||05-16-2001||11:21 PM||||if my 3.4 will not go any faster.  i will put a NOS kit on it and just blow it to the ground.  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||05-16-2001||11:47 PM||||OK that last post lost me.  One min. were talking like a reg. NOS kit then we get into accessories I dunno.<P>So, my question is, I just want a 50-70 shot.  Nothing fancy but I would be willing to spend more for a better kit.  Which is the best kit for what I want?  Don't need some dual stage super duper blah blah blah, just a good system for 50-70 range.<P>I won't ever use it unless I am racing so its not like I will need a 15lb. bottle. ||||reg||5
Z||000012||fropuff||05-17-2001||08:04 AM||||I agree with you, Black88GT.  I would only use my system maybe 3-4 times a week at the maximum.  Now all I want is the 70 shot dry kit, the one that is around $450.  Not the wet kit, or whatever it is, even though it probably is better.  I also want to do the minimum amount of modifications to the car, other than the performance pulley and shift kit, and the cold air intake.  I plan on getting the MSD box and cleaning the injectors, but I think that's about all I need.  Thanks for the replies; I appreciate them.  Keep em comin!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000013||1FST2M6||05-17-2001||02:27 PM||||the wet kit is better, it requires let attention and is WAY safer than a dry kit. the WET kit is only $449... <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>  i had a dry kit.. and it was ok. but wet is better! and for the same price.. why waste your $.. get the best the first time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
